     [38;5;246mlocalhost/127.0.0.1 -> local API, a staging host -> staging API, everything else -> the current [39m
     [38;5;246mhttps://api.example.com. Safe for unrecognized hosts; risks a dev machine silently hitting prod.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m local + staging + prod, default local
     [38;5;246mSame table, but an unrecognized hostname falls back to the local API. A misconfigured deploy fails loudly instead [39m
     [38;5;246mof quietly talking to prod.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m local + prod only
     [38;5;246mJust localhost vs everything else. Smallest table; add staging when a staging host actually exists.[39m
